/-!
# Finite type descends along fpqc coverings

A quasi-coherent module on a scheme is of finite type as soon as its pullback to every member
of an fpqc covering is of finite type.

The statement is local on the base, so it suffices to treat an affine base. There a
quasi-compact fpqc covering is refined by a finite family of affine schemes flat over the base;
their coproduct is affine, flat and surjective over the base, hence faithfully flat on global
sections, and finiteness of modules descends along a faithfully flat ring map. Assembling the
affine pieces uses that a module generated by finitely many sections on each member of an open
cover is of finite type.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqc`: finite type of a quasi-coherent module
  descends along an fpqc covering.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteType_of_pullback_of_flat_surjective`: the same for a single flat,
  surjective, quasi-compact morphism, which is a one-member fpqc covering.

## Implementation notes

An fpqc covering is expressed as membership of its family of arrows in
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage`, and pullback of modules is Mathlib's
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.pullback`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AZ)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

universe w u v

open CategoryTheory
open CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange
open scoped TensorProduct

/-- Being of finite type is invariant under isomorphism, with the hypothesis supplied
explicitly rather than by instance search. -/
lemma isFiniteType_of_iso {X : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules} (e : M ≅ N)
    (h : M.IsFiniteType) : N.IsFiniteType :=
  have := h
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} e

/-- Finite type for a quasi-coherent module descends along an fpqc covering, with the covering
given as a family of morphisms rather than as a `Scheme.Cover` and with quasi-coherence as an
explicit hypothesis. This is the unbundled form of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FlatBaseChange.isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqcCover`. -/
public lemma isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqc {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules)
    (hF : F.IsQuasicoherent) {ι : Type w} (X' : ι → Scheme.{u})
    (f : ∀ i, X' i ⟶ X)
    (hcover : Presieve.ofArrows X' f ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage X)
    (hfinite : ∀ i, ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (f i)).obj F).IsFiniteType) :
    F.IsFiniteType :=
  have : F.IsQuasicoherent := hF
  isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqcCover F
    { I₀ := ι
      X := X'
      f := f
      mem₀ := by simpa using hcover }
    hfinite

/-- A quasi-coherent module whose pullback along a single flat, surjective, quasi-compact
morphism is of finite type is itself of finite type. Such a morphism is a one-member fpqc
covering of its target. -/
public theorem isFiniteType_of_pullback_of_flat_surjective
    {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y) [Flat f] [Surjective f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (M : Y.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent]
    (h : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback f).obj M).IsFiniteType) :
    M.IsFiniteType :=
  isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqcCover M
    { CategoryTheory.PreZeroHypercover.singleton.{0} f with
      mem₀ := by simp }
    fun _ => h

end AlgebraicGeometry
